## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical data ingestion resilience, including handling mixed encodings and multi-channel sources (SFTP for CSVs, REST for JSON), along with end-to-end lineage and data quality understanding.

## Key Concepts
- Encoding detection and transcoding at ingestion
- Incremental loading using per-file watermarks
- Mapping Data Flows for Parquet conversion and star schema population in Azure Synapse
- Data quality and schema validation checks
- Purview lineage integration for traceability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to detect encoding and transcode to UTF-8
const fs = require('fs');
module.exports = async function (context, myBlob) {
    const buffer = Buffer.from(myBlob);
    const isUtf16 = buffer[0] === 0xFF && buffer[1] === 0xFE;
    let content;

    if (isUtf16) {
        content = buffer.toString('utf16le');
    } else {
        content = buffer.toString('utf8');
    }

    context.bindings.outputBlob = content;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of mixed-format ingestion, format detection, and unifying to a common schema. Also evaluates basic Data Flow usage, incremental loads, drift tolerance, lineage, and simple quality checks.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Data Factory: format detection and routing
- Mapping Data Flows: transform CSV and Parquet into a unified schema
- Incremental loads: upserts to avoid full refreshes
- Purview lineage: tracking data from landing to Synapse
- Basic data quality: row counts, duplicates, null checks

## Code Example
```json
{
  "name": "FormatDetection",
  "type": "IfCondition",
  "conditions": [
    { "expression": "@equals(pipeline().parameters.fileType, 'CSV')" }
  ],
  "branches": {
    "CSVPath": {
      "source": {"type": "DelimitedTextSource", "delimiter": ",", "header": true},
      "sink": {"type": "SynapseSink", "table": "stg_partner_csv"}
    },
    "ParquetPath": {
      "source": {"type": "ParquetSource"},
      "sink": {"type": "SynapseSink", "table": "stg_partner_parquet"}
    }
  }
}
```

